WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.020
Dean and Sam Winchester. Mulder and Scully.&nbsp;
Wednesday and Thing. Every supernatural crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.400
solver needs a partner to back them up when&nbsp;
their back is against the wall, and it turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.100
out that being a disembodied hand comes in, well,&nbsp;
handy quite frequently. It also turns out that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.840
was an impressive feat to capture the effect on&nbsp;
film. Keep watching to find out how they did it.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.680
Though Wednesday Addams did not intend&nbsp;
on careening down a rabbit hole when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.060
first enrolled in Nevermore Academy, fate&nbsp;
had other plans. The events of "Wednesday"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.960
kick off upon the titular character's&nbsp;
immediate expulsion from High School.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.040
Morticia and Gomez Addams ship her off&nbsp;
to where she can be among her peers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.860
a school for bizarre adolescents. Wednesday&nbsp;
fully intends on continuing her anti-social ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.240
but this all changes when she sees a fellow&nbsp;
student murdered by a strange monster.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.160
With the help of a childhood assistant,&nbsp;
Wednesday is on the case. At first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.520
Thing's contribution is slightly&nbsp;
unwilling as Wednesday treats him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.560
like an insubordinate employee. But after a&nbsp;
time, Wednesday's walls fall and they become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.600
true allies. Fans of the Tim Burton series&nbsp;
quickly became enamored with Thing, taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.940
to social media to praise Wednesday's helpful&nbsp;
and empathetic friend. One Reddit user wrote,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.740
"Thing is brilliant. I love that Wednesday&nbsp;
has this one part of her family with her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.180
so she's never really alone."

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.780
"Wednesday" may be a modernized&nbsp;
version of the popular franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.860
but the Netflix series still involves&nbsp;
the classic hallmarks that delight fans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.060
It isn't long after Wednesday settles into&nbsp;
school that she discovers she isn't alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.920
Thing first follows her at the behest of her&nbsp;
parents but soon joins her wild crusade with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.720
his handsy skills. It may seem that the severed&nbsp;
appendage is only the result of computer graphics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.920
but that would be doing the man behind the&nbsp;
hand — Victor Dorobantu — a disservice.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.720
Netflix revealed on Twitter that Thing&nbsp;
is portrayed by Dorobantu, who wears a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.460
full-bodied blue suit to get the effect. With his&nbsp;
many scenes getting into hard-to-reach places,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:59.520
the actor must contort and many times crawl on&nbsp;
the ground to get the shots needed. Dorobantu even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.740
showed a video on his personal Instagram about the&nbsp;
process of filming one specific underwater scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.120
While these efforts may seem tedious, there&nbsp;
is no doubt that it ultimately gets results.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.460
Wednesday would never be one to admit it, but&nbsp;
she needs Thing. Her antisocial schtick only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.860
gets her so far, and Thing represents a support&nbsp;
system that never judges her. From sneaking her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.820
into morgues to getting her a dress for the&nbsp;
dance, Thing has proven his devotion to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.600
spooky mistress, making him one of the&nbsp;
most likable characters in "Wednesday."

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.820
Victor Dorobantu's behind-the-scenes photos&nbsp;
as Thing have taken the internet by storm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.400
with many praising the actor for his difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.600
role. "SNL" alum Laraine Newman&nbsp;
took to Twitter in awe, saying,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.840
"I'm sincerely marveling at&nbsp;
the actor playing Thing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.380
Netflix's Wednesday ... Victor&nbsp;
Dorobantu's work is stunning."

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:51.120
With Dorobantu on everyone's mind,&nbsp;
one can't help but wonder: who is he?

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.100
In the wake of Thing's popularity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:58.500
Dorobantu discussed his "Wednesday" role in&nbsp;
a candid chat with Vanity Fair. The 25 year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.680
old magician had this to say about&nbsp;
the viral behind-the-scenes photos,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.400
"I didn't know we had so many&nbsp;
photos of me behind the scenes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.920
It's kind of interesting to see that even for me."

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:13.800
Would fans believe that "Wednesday" is Dorobantu's&nbsp;
first acting gig? A closeup magician by trade in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.000
his native Romania, Dorobantu ended&nbsp;
up at a casting house in Bucharest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.020
where he was chosen as a finalist for&nbsp;
the role amongst two other magicians.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.220
What nabbed him the role? The magician&nbsp;
has no idea. The actor told the outlet,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.520
"I wish that Tim [Burton] would&nbsp;
tell me what he saw in me."

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.140
What the trickster does know is that he and&nbsp;
the series creator got along swimmingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.220
recounting how his hand began to take&nbsp;
on a life of its own on a table while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.680
chatting with Burton for the first time. He said,

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.800
"So I guess Tim saw in front of him an actor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.280
the hand separately. So it was a&nbsp;
connection from the first moment."

